    public static func sorted<Row>(
        _ rows: [Row],
        by comparator: (Row, Row) -> ComparisonResult,
        ascending: Bool
    ) -> [Row]
}
```

### **TSDataTable<Row>** (lines 56–304)
```swift
public struct TSDataTable<Row: Identifiable>: View {
    public init(
        rows: [Row],
        columns: [TSColumn<Row>],
        selection: Binding<Set<Row.ID>> = .constant([]),
        density: TSTableDensity = .standard
    )
    
    // Add expandable detail row:
    public func rowDetail(@ViewBuilder _ content: @escaping (Row) -> some View) -> TSDataTable
}
```

**Adaptive Layout:**
- **Regular (macOS / iPad):** Columnar grid with sortable headers, row selection checkboxes, optional expand chevrons
- **Compact (iPhone):** Card list via `TSCard`, same row/column info displayed vertically
- **States:** All rows rendered with optional per-row expansion; selection bulk bar at top when items selected

